{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"**Cause**  \n- `publish()` stores a list of similarity scores (`similar`) generated by `similarity()`.  \n- `similarity()` returns a **float**.  \n- When the DynamoDB table is empty the first write stores an empty `similar` list, so no float reaches DynamoDB and the operation succeeds.  \n- On the second publish the `similar` list contains float scores, and DynamoDB raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` → 500 response.\n\n**Fix**  \n- Imported `Decimal` from the standard library.  \n- Updated `related()` to coerce each similarity score to `Decimal` before adding it to the item (using `Decimal(str(...))`).  \n- Added a detailed docstring explaining the DynamoDB float limitation and why the conversion is needed.  \n- No other behavior changed; the API now consistently succeeds on every publish.\n\n**Applied parts of the colleague’s note**  \n- Identified the *“Float types are not supported”* DynamoDB error and traced it to the similarity scores.  \n- Recognized that the first‑write path (empty `similar` list) masks the bug, matching the note’s description of a state‑dependent failure.  \n- Implemented the single‑line fix (convert to `Decimal`), as suggested.  \n\nThe repository now passes all tests and the publish endpoint no longer fails on the second call."}}
